@page "/features"
@attribute [ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]
@layout MarketingLayout

<PageTitle>Features · Drive-In Online</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Everything Drive-In Online does for your drive-in: spot-by-spot online sales, gate check-in and sales, double features, pricing, staff roles and more." />
</HeadContent>

<MarketingNav />
<PageHero Eyebrow="Features" Title="Built for the drive-in"
          Lede="Not a cinema seat-picker with cars bolted on: every part is designed around lots, spots, carloads and double features." />

<main class="wrap page">
    <div class="prose">
        <h2>Sell tickets by the spot</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>A live map of your lot.</strong> Guests choose their exact spot on each screen's layout. Everyone sees spots fill up in real time.</li>
            <li><strong>No double-selling.</strong> A spot is held for the guest while they pay; if two people pick the same spot, the first one gets it and the other is asked to choose again.</li>
            <li><strong>Card checkout</strong> with your ticket options and add-ons, and an emailed receipt with a QR code and a 4-character gate code.</li>
            <li><strong>Tickets are good for their showing only,</strong> and your no-refunds policy is stated at checkout and on every receipt.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Run the gate</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Check cars in fast:</strong> scan the QR code with a handheld scanner or a phone camera, or type the gate code the driver reads out. Tickets for another date, or already used, are flagged.</li>
            <li><strong>Sell to drive-ups</strong> from the same screen: pick today's showing and a spot, take the card on your terminal, and the car is checked in. Gate sales keep going after the movie starts.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Screens, spots and the schedule</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Up to four screens, each with its own rows of spots and labeling (B7, 2G or 207).</li>
            <li>A lot map that shows every screen around your concession stand.</li>
            <li>Single films or double (even quadruple) features with intermissions, in your time zone, and an operating season with opening and closing dates.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Pricing your way</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Price schedules like "1 occupant", "2 occupants" or "Car load", with a different schedule for special showings.</li>
            <li>Add-ons: fees such as outside food, and dollar or percent discounts for seniors or veterans.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your crew</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Invite employees by email and give them roles: box office, gate, operations, manager.</li>
            <li>Choose exactly which actions each role can take; staff can never grant more than they have.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Coming soon</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Concessions ordering from the car <span class="soon">Coming soon</span></li>
            <li>Nightly sales and attendance reporting <span class="soon">Coming soon</span></li>
            <li>Announcements to your regulars <span class="soon">Coming soon</span></li>
        </ul>

        <p style="margin-top: 32px"><a class="cta cta-bulb" href="get-started">Start your free demo</a> <a class="cta cta-outline" href="pricing">See pricing</a></p>
    </div>
</main>

<MarketingFooter />
